# Git workflow

Never commit feature work directly to `main`. Flow: `main` → `develop` → `feature/<name>` → PR → `develop` → `main`.

Inspect `git status` and the current branch before Git changes. Never discard user work, force-push, hard-reset, or delete branches unless the user explicitly asks.

Conventional commits: `feat:`, `fix:`, `refactor:`, `test:`, `chore:`. Keep commits small and logical. Do not commit unless asked.

Do not rename existing folders/files unless requested.
